            <ArticleTitle>Continuous six-month infusion of intravenous nitroglycerin in a patient awaiting cardiac transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1470-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a patient with ischemic cardiomyopathy who was treated with a continuous high dose infusion of intravenous nitroglycerin for six months while awaiting cardiac transplantation. Surprisingly, methemoglobinemia did not develop and nitroglycerin continued to be clinically effective in relieving angina during the six-month period. We believe this to be the first reported instance of the safe use of such prolonged infusion of intravenous nitroglycerin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
